==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|spedily}}, {{m|enm|spedili}}, from {{inh|en|ang|*spēdiġlīċe}}, {{m|ang|ġespēdiġlīċe||prosperously}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|speedy|ly}}. Cognate with {{cog|sco|spedely}}, {{m|sco|spedelie||quickly, speedily}}. Compare also {{cog|ang|spēdlīċe||effectually, effectively, successfully, efficaciously, powerfully, in a manner which produces a result}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈspiːdɪli/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-speedily.wav|Audio (UK)}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|er|more}}

# In a [[speedy]] or [[fast]] manner.
#* {{quote-journal|1=en|year=1899|month=Feb|author=Joseph Conrad|authorlink=Joseph Conrad|title=The Heart of Darkness|journal=Blackwood's Edinburgh Magazine|page=205|passage=He was '''speedily''' reassured, and with a large, white, rascally grin, and a glance at his charge, seemed to take me into partnership in his exalted trust.}}

